DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("((x)^(1/4))^2-2*(10/(x))+1");
$fun_1 = Formula("e^(((x/6)*1))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(-infinity, 11] U [1, 7] U (-infinity, 11]");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("[1, 7] U (-infinity, 11] U (-infinity, 11]");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("[1, 7] - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((-infinity, 11])) U [1, 7]");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(2, infinity) U ((2, infinity) U ((3, 8)) U (-infinity, 13))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("((((-infinity, 13))) U (-infinity, 13) U (2, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 13)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((3, 8)))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("(2, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (3, 8)) U (2, infinity) U (((3, 8)))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`15.55+7.53-1+18.37`] is equal to [_____]{40.45}
---

[`8+8.78+7.28/19`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>17.1631578947,width=>7}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 13\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 3 < x < 8\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x > 1\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup (C \cup (B) \cup A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(((A)) \cup A \cup C) \cap A \cap (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`C \cap B \cup C \cup ((B)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 11\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`B \cap (A) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 7, 2, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 2, 9, -2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, 9, -2>") x Compute("<7, 2, -3>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, 2, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, 2, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 2, -3>") . Compute("<2, 9, -2>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 1, 10, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -1, -5, 4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, 10, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -5, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -5, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, 10, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, 10, -1>") x Compute("<-1, -5, 4>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
